MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The microSD card fits my Raspberry Pi experimentation because a separate card would let me try another image conveniently, after checking compatibility.",
    "The powered USB hub fits my desk setup because it could organize several peripherals and let me switch accessories off individually. The card reader also serves a clear purpose for writing Raspberry Pi images, though I would choose the standalone card this time."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The streaming players, Echo Dot, and smart plug do not address my current computer and networking tasks; owning electronics does not mean I currently want streaming or voice-control devices.",
    "The Ethernet switch relates to my recent networking purchases, but 24 ports exceeds my needs. The SSD would require a planned upgrade and compatibility checks, while another HDMI cable offers no clear benefit when I already have one."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My electronics purchases seem to have been treated as broad interest in household gadgets, even when those gadgets serve different purposes from my current projects.",
    "Past purchases of cables and storage seem to have been taken as reasons to suggest more of them, without enough attention to whether I need a replacement, extra capacity, or a different function."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent Ethernet adapter, patch cables, headphone mount, and duster point toward practical computer setup and maintenance needs.",
    "A useful next purchase needs a specific role alongside what I already own. Another card can support a separate Raspberry Pi image, but a second HDMI cable or two overlapping card options would need an additional reason."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognized my computer accessory interests but stretched them into unrelated gadgets and upgrades without a clear current purpose."
}
